---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const releases = await getCollection('music');
const singles = releases
  .filter((r) => r.data.kind !== 'playlist')
  .sort((a, b) => (a.data.track ?? 99) - (b.data.track ?? 99));
const playlist = releases.find((r) => r.data.kind === 'playlist');

const stories = [
  'The elevator descends and the night begins with a bad decision, made quietly and on purpose. "One more sip" is the promise the whole album keeps.',
  'A rule is set early: whatever happens tonight, morning erases the names. That deadline is what makes every hour after it burn brighter.',
  'Under a streetlight, the lies that only work at 2am. Both of them know. Neither of them stops.',
  'The deepest point of the night. Neon rippling on the water, bass under the skin — not sinking, surrendering.',
  'A convenience-store window, a coffee going cold, a phone that stays dark. Hope is at its most stubborn at 3am.',
  'The goodbye that tastes like the first lie of the night. Everything after this is aftermath.',
  'One song loops until the sky turns pale — and the last line hands you back to track one. The night never really ends.',
];
const scenes = singles.map((s, i) => ({ song: s, story: stories[i] ?? '' }));
---

<Base title="One Night Loop — the SHINYA album story" description="Seven tracks, one night: how the SHINYA album loops from midnight back to midnight.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="page-banner">
      <img class="page-banner-art" src={`${base}/${playlist?.data.poster ?? 'images/hero-character.jpg'}`} alt="" />
      <div class="page-banner-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="page-banner-inner">
        <h1 class="page-banner-title">ONE NIGHT LOOP</h1>
        <p class="page-banner-sub">Seven tracks · one night · no exit</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose about-intro">
      <p>
        The SHINYA album is one night told in order. It starts at midnight with a bad decision,
        goes down as far as a night can go, and ends where it began. Walk it track by track:
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section scenes">
      {scenes.map(({ song, story }, i) => (
        <div class={`scene ${i % 2 === 1 ? 'flip' : ''}`}>
          <div class="scene-visual">
            {song.data.poster && <img src={`${base}/${song.data.poster}`} alt={song.data.title} loading="lazy" />}
            <span class="scene-time">TRACK 0{song.data.track}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="scene-text">
            <h3>{song.data.title}{song.data.titleEn ? ` — ${song.data.titleEn}` : ''}</h3>
            <p>{story}</p>
            <p><a href={`${base}/music/${song.id}/`}>Lyrics & video →</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="section prose about-outro">
      <p>
        And then 4:59 rolls over, the elevator numbers start falling again, and 毒でいいの is
        already playing. The album is a loop because those nights are a loop.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hear it in one sitting: <a href={`${base}/music/`}>the 60-minute SHINYA mix</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
